{%- comment -%}
  App showcase — 3D phone mockups that drift as you scroll.

  Three deliberate implementation choices, because the obvious versions of this
  are all bad:

  1. **The 3D is CSS, not a rendered image.** A perspective transform on a real
     <img> stays crisp at every screen density, weighs nothing extra, and can be
     re-shot by swapping a PNG. Pre-rendered 3D mockups (Rotato and friends) bake
     the angle and the resolution in, and every future screenshot means going
     back to the tool.

  2. **The parallax uses `animation-timeline: view()`** — native scroll-driven
     animation, which the browser runs off the main thread. The usual approach,
     a scroll listener writing transforms, runs on the main thread and janks on
     exactly the mid-range Android and older iPhones our buyers actually hold.
     Browsers without it get the layout with no motion, which is fine.

  3. **No scroll-jacking, and `prefers-reduced-motion` kills all of it.** Motion
     here is decoration; the page has to read perfectly with none of it. Anyone
     who has asked their OS for less movement gets a clean static layout, not a
     degraded one.

  The device frame is drawn in CSS — bezel, rounded corners, screen inset — so
  the source images can be plain screenshots straight off a phone.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- assign motion = section.settings.motion -%}

<section class="showcase full-width{% if section.settings.tone == 'dark' %} showcase--dark{% endif %}">
  <div class="showcase-inner">
    <header class="showcase-head">
      {%- if section.settings.label != blank -%}
        <p class="showcase-label">{{ section.settings.label }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}
      <h2 class="showcase-title">{{ section.settings.title }}</h2>
      {%- if section.settings.intro != blank -%}
        <div class="showcase-intro">{{ section.settings.intro }}</div>
      {%- endif -%}
    </header>

    <div class="showcase-rail" data-motion="{{ motion }}">
      {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          Depth alternates 1/2/3 across the blocks so adjacent phones travel at
          visibly different rates. Uniform parallax reads as the whole section
          sliding, which looks like a rendering fault rather than depth.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- assign depth = forloop.index0 | modulo: 3 | plus: 1 -%}
        <figure
          class="device device--d{{ depth }}"
          data-depth="{{ depth }}"
          {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
        >
          <div class="device-frame">
            <div class="device-notch" aria-hidden="true"></div>
            {%- comment -%}
              Two image sources, on purpose.

              `image` is the theme-editor picker and always wins — it is how
              Henry swaps a screenshot without touching code. But a picker
              stores a Shopify file reference, which cannot be written into a
              JSON template, so shipping working defaults needs a second route:
              `asset_name`, a plain filename in assets/. That lets the section
              arrive populated instead of arriving as six empty boxes nobody
              gets around to filling.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <div class="device-screen">
              {%- if block.settings.image != blank -%}
                <img
                  src="{{ block.settings.image | image_url: width: 640 }}"
                  alt="{{ block.settings.image.alt | default: block.settings.caption | escape }}"
                  width="320"
                  height="693"
                  loading="lazy"
                  decoding="async"
                  sizes="(min-width: 900px) 22vw, 60vw"
                  srcset="
                    {{ block.settings.image | image_url: width: 320 }} 320w,
                    {{ block.settings.image | image_url: width: 640 }} 640w
                  "
                >
              {%- elsif block.settings.asset_name != blank -%}
                {%- comment -%}
                  The `w` descriptors below are MEASURED widths, not the numbers
                  handed to asset_img_url, and the difference is the whole point.

                  `asset_img_url: 'NxN'` fits the image inside an N-by-N box, so
                  on a tall portrait screenshot the HEIGHT binds and the width
                  lands far short of N. Measured against the live CDN for a
                  640x1387 source:

                      _320x  -> 295x640        _640x  -> 295x640
                      _720x  -> 640x1387       _1024x -> 640x1387

                  Declaring that first one as "640w" told the browser a 295px
                  image was 640px wide, so it confidently chose the small file
                  for a 2x display and the screens rendered soft. Honest
                  descriptors let it pick correctly.
                {%- endcomment -%}
                <img
                  src="{{ block.settings.asset_name | asset_img_url: '720x' }}"
                  alt="{{ block.settings.alt | default: block.settings.caption | escape }}"
                  width="640"
                  height="1387"
                  loading="lazy"
                  decoding="async"
                  sizes="(min-width: 900px) 22vw, 45vw"
                  srcset="
                    {{ block.settings.asset_name | asset_img_url: '640x' }} 295w,
                    {{ block.settings.asset_name | asset_img_url: '720x' }} 640w
                  "
                >
              {%- else -%}
                <span class="device-placeholder" aria-hidden="true">{{ forloop.index }}</span>
              {%- endif -%}
            </div>
          </div>

          {%- if block.settings.caption != blank or block.settings.feature != blank -%}
            <figcaption class="device-cap">
              {%- if block.settings.feature != blank -%}
                <span class="device-feature">{{ block.settings.feature }}</span>
              {%- endif -%}
              {%- if block.settings.caption != blank -%}
                <span class="device-caption">{{ block.settings.caption }}</span>
              {%- endif -%}
            </figcaption>
          {%- endif -%}
        </figure>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{% stylesheet %}
  .showcase {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: var(--content-grid);
    background: var(--bg);
    padding-block: clamp(72px, 10vw, 128px);
    overflow: clip; /* parallax can push a phone past the edge; never scroll the page sideways */
  }

  .showcase--dark { background: var(--bg2); }
  .showcase-inner { grid-column: 2; }

  .showcase-head {
    max-width: 46rem;
    margin-block-end: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4.5rem);
  }

  .showcase-label {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.18em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--green);
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
  }

  .showcase-title {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 5.5vw, 3.5rem);
    line-height: 0.95;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
    color: var(--white);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .showcase-intro {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-block-start: 1rem;
  }

  .showcase-intro p { margin: 0; }

  /* --- the rail --------------------------------------------------------- */

  /* Two columns on a phone, not one.
     `auto-fit` with a 12rem minimum collapsed to a single column at 375px,
     which stacked four full-height mockups into a 3,260px section — about four
     screens of scrolling to get past one idea. Explicit columns instead. */
  .showcase-rail {
    display: grid;
    gap: clamp(1.25rem, 4vw, 3rem);
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    /* The shared perspective origin is what makes the phones read as one
       scene rather than as several separately-tilted pictures. */
    perspective: 1600px;
    perspective-origin: 50% 40%;
  }

  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .showcase-rail { grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); align-items: start; }
  }

  /* --- the device ------------------------------------------------------- */

  .device {
    margin: 0;
    transform-style: preserve-3d;
    will-change: transform;
  }

  .device-frame {
    position: relative;
    border-radius: 2rem;
    padding: 0.5rem;
    background: linear-gradient(160deg, #2a2f2b 0%, #12160f 55%, #23282a 100%);
    box-shadow:
      0 1px 0 rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.14) inset,
      0 30px 60px -20px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.85),
      0 8px 20px -8px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.6);
    transform: rotateY(var(--ry, -14deg)) rotateX(var(--rx, 5deg));
    transition: transform 350ms ease-out;
  }

  /* Mirror the tilt across the rail so the set converges on the centre
     instead of all leaning the same way like a row of dominoes. */
  .device:nth-child(even) .device-frame { --ry: 14deg; }

  .device:hover .device-frame,
  .device:focus-within .device-frame { --ry: 0deg; --rx: 0deg; }

  .device-notch {
    position: absolute;
    top: 0.5rem;
    left: 50%;
    transform: translateX(-50%);
    width: 32%;
    height: 0.85rem;
    background: #0a0d08;
    border-radius: 0 0 0.6rem 0.6rem;
    z-index: 2;
  }

  .device-screen {
    position: relative;
    border-radius: 1.6rem;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: var(--bg);
    aspect-ratio: 886 / 1920;
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
  }

  .device-screen img {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
    display: block;
  }

  .device-placeholder {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 2.5rem;
    color: var(--border);
  }

  .device-cap {
    margin-block-start: 1.15rem;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.3rem;
  }

  .device-feature {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.66rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--green);
  }

  .device-caption {
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  /* --- motion ----------------------------------------------------------- */

  /* Native scroll-driven parallax. Off the main thread, so it cannot jank the
     way a scroll listener does. Browsers without support simply get no motion. */
  @supports (animation-timeline: view()) {
    .showcase-rail[data-motion="parallax"] .device,
    .showcase-rail[data-motion="both"] .device {
      animation: device-drift linear both;
      animation-timeline: view();
      animation-range: entry 0% exit 100%;
    }

    .device--d1 { --drift: 26px; }
    .device--d2 { --drift: 52px; }
    .device--d3 { --drift: 14px; }

    @keyframes device-drift {
      from { translate: 0 var(--drift); }
      to   { translate: 0 calc(var(--drift) * -1); }
    }
  }

  /* A slow idle float, so the phones are alive even before you scroll. */
  .showcase-rail[data-motion="float"] .device-frame,
  .showcase-rail[data-motion="both"] .device-frame {
    animation: device-float 7s ease-in-out infinite alternate;
  }

  .showcase-rail .device:nth-child(2) .device-frame { animation-delay: -2.3s; }
  .showcase-rail .device:nth-child(3) .device-frame { animation-delay: -4.1s; }
  .showcase-rail .device:nth-child(4) .device-frame { animation-delay: -1.2s; }

  @keyframes device-float {
    from { transform: rotateY(var(--ry, -14deg)) rotateX(var(--rx, 5deg)) translateY(-6px); }
    to   { transform: rotateY(var(--ry, -14deg)) rotateX(var(--rx, 5deg)) translateY(6px); }
  }

  /* Decoration only. Asked for less motion, get none — and get a flat, honest
     layout rather than a broken-looking one. */
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .showcase-rail .device,
    .showcase-rail .device-frame {
      animation: none !important;
      transition: none !important;
    }
    .device-frame { transform: none; }
  }

  /* Below ~700px the tilt costs legibility on an already-small screenshot,
     so the phones stand square and only the drift remains. */
  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .device-frame { --ry: 0deg; --rx: 0deg; }
    .showcase-rail { perspective: none; }
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "App showcase",
  "tag": "section",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "text", "id": "label", "label": "Eyebrow", "default": "The app" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "title", "label": "Heading", "default": "It does the editing" },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "intro",
      "label": "Intro",
      "default": "<p>Free on the App Store, and it works whether or not you ever buy the kit.</p>"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "motion",
      "label": "Motion",
      "options": [
        { "value": "none", "label": "Static" },
        { "value": "float", "label": "Gentle float" },
        { "value": "parallax", "label": "Parallax on scroll" },
        { "value": "both", "label": "Float and parallax" }
      ],
      "default": "both",
      "info": "Anyone whose device asks for reduced motion gets a static layout regardless. Parallax uses native scroll-driven animation, so it runs off the main thread and will not stutter."
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "tone",
      "label": "Background",
      "options": [
        { "value": "light", "label": "Base" },
        { "value": "dark", "label": "Raised" }
      ],
      "default": "dark"
    }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "screen",
      "name": "App screen",
      "settings": [
        { "type": "image_picker", "id": "image", "label": "Screenshot", "info": "A plain phone screenshot. The device frame is drawn in CSS around it. Overrides the asset filename below." },
        { "type": "text", "id": "asset_name", "label": "…or a theme asset filename", "info": "e.g. clippar-app-live-recording.png, uploaded to the theme's assets. Used only when no screenshot is picked above." },
        { "type": "text", "id": "alt", "label": "Alt text", "info": "Describe the screen and what it is doing. Only used with the asset filename; a picked image carries its own." },
        { "type": "text", "id": "feature", "label": "Feature label", "default": "Feature" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "caption", "label": "Caption", "default": "What this screen does." }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "max_blocks": 6,
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "App showcase",
      "blocks": [
        { "type": "screen", "settings": { "feature": "Live recording", "caption": "Pick your course, set the scorecard, and start. The clicker does the rest." } },
        { "type": "screen", "settings": { "feature": "Shot detection", "caption": "Finds the swing inside each recording and throws away the walk-up." } },
        { "type": "screen", "settings": { "feature": "The reel", "caption": "Every shot, trimmed and in order, before you reach the car park." } },
        { "type": "screen", "settings": { "feature": "Your rounds", "caption": "Filter by course, hole or date. No scrolling the camera roll." } }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
